Cast between closure types with a functional cast, not reinterpret_cast.

A Borland __closure is a built-in (code, data) pair, so reinterpret_cast
between two closure types is allowed. Under standard C++ a closure is a
class, and reinterpret_cast cannot convert one class object into another.
The functional cast is the old C-style cast this line had before upstream's
"Refactoring old-style casts" (e5efed895), so C++Builder compiles it as it
did then; the shim gives it the same meaning, keeping the original closure
so the cast back is lossless. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/Terminal.cpp	2026-10-11 16:55:31.730293582 -0300
+++ b/source/core/Terminal.cpp	2026-10-11 16:55:31.734293597 -0300
@@ -4178,7 +4178,7 @@
               else
               {
                 // not used anymore
-                TProcessFileEventEx ProcessFileEx = reinterpret_cast<TProcessFileEventEx>(ProcessFile);
+                TProcessFileEventEx ProcessFileEx = TProcessFileEventEx(ProcessFile);
                 ProcessFileEx(FileName, File, Param, Index);
               }
               Success = true;
